Please generate me a basic SVG for a technical talk that visualizes the slide
"What does a VMM need to create a VM?" (see 03-background.md), similar in style
to from-host-vmm-process-to-vm-guest.svg. Keep it simple, high-level and
approachable:

- The VMM provides a virtual device, e.g. a virtio-blk disk, sitting in a
  virtual PCI bus that the VMM emulates (show a second, faded device such as
  virtio-net so the bus is visible)
- The guest sees it as a normal PCI device (slot 00:04.0, virtio-blk) and
  writes to it as usual; keep it light on PCI details: slot yes, no BARs,
  no config space, no addresses
- Every such access is an MMIO write that is trapped by KVM and forwarded
  back to the VMM
- The VMM implements the device and does the real work, e.g. writing into a
  disk.img file on the host
- Take-away: virtual hardware is just software in the VMM
